    summary: "Frank McCormick is Professor at the UCSF Helen Diller Family Comprehensive Cancer Center and former Scientific Lead of the RAS Initiative at the National Cancer Institute (NIH). A molecular biologist who has worked on RAS signalling for four decades, he founded Onyx Pharmaceuticals, the company behind the origins of sorafenib and carfilzomib, and served as scientific lead of the NCI RAS Initiative at Frederick National Laboratory. His papers include a Clinical Cancer Research review of KRAS as a therapeutic target and a Cancer Cell commentary on covalent KRAS inhibitors entering the clinic. His work on KRAS and RAS inhibitors bears on pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma, colorectal cancer and non-small-cell lung cancer.",
