    id: "owen-witte", kind: "person", asOf, name: "Owen N. Witte", role: "University Professor; Founding Director Emeritus, Broad Stem Cell Research Center, UCLA", institutionId: "ucla-jonsson", institutions: ["ucla-jonsson"],
    specialisms: ["Prostate cancer biology", "Kinase signalling", "Immunotherapy targets"],
    tldr: "Discovered the BCR-ABL kinase activity that imatinib blocks and now hunts for new prostate cancer targets.",
    summary: "Owen Witte is University Professor and Founding Director Emeritus of the Broad Stem Cell Research Center at UCLA, within the UCLA Jonsson Comprehensive Cancer Center. A molecular biologist specialising in prostate cancer biology and kinase signalling, he identified the tyrosine kinase activity of the BCR-ABL oncoprotein, the basis of imatinib. His papers include the Cell report that an alteration of the human c-abl protein in K562 leukaemia cells unmasks associated tyrosine kinase activity and a Science study reprogramming normal human epithelial tissues to a common, lethal neuroendocrine cancer lineage. His laboratory now defines prostate cancer lineage plasticity and hunts for immunotherapy targets such as PSCA and STEAP1, alongside PSMA and the androgen receptor.",
