    summary: "Stephen Forman is Director of the Hematologic Malignancies Research Institute and Francis and Kathleen McNamara Distinguished Chair at City of Hope. A haematologist specialising in haematopoietic cell transplantation, CAR-T and lymphoma, he led City of Hope's bone marrow transplant programme for decades and built its cell therapy programme, one of the largest in the country. His papers include a Blood report of phase 1 studies of central memory-derived CD19 CAR T-cell therapy after autologous transplant in B-cell non-Hodgkin lymphoma and a Blood commentary on the myth of the second remission of acute leukaemia in adults. He directs haematologic malignancies research including CAR-T development for lymphoma and leukaemia and off-the-shelf cell therapy.",
