    summary: "Sara Hurvitz is Senior Vice President and Director of the Clinical Research Division at Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center and Head of the Division of Hematology and Oncology at the University of Washington, having moved from UCLA in 2023. A breast medical oncologist specialising in HER2 and antibody-drug conjugates, she was principal investigator of DESTINY-Breast03, the trial in which trastuzumab deruxtecan was compared with trastuzumab emtansine, and of many HER2-directed and CDK4/6 studies. Her papers report the updated results of DESTINY-Breast03 in the Lancet and the KRISTINE phase 3 trial of neoadjuvant trastuzumab, pertuzumab and chemotherapy versus trastuzumab emtansine plus pertuzumab in Lancet Oncology. Her work spans HER2-positive, HR-positive and triple-negative breast cancer.",
